{"custom_id":"s-ap_physics_c_mechanics-m05-k2-q2","ok":true,"model":"claude-opus-5-5","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDGupqvujetBcMgU4c1o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph shows one full period of 4 s, so the period is T = 4 s.\n\n1. Angular frequency: ω = 2π/T = 2π/4 = π/2 ≈ 1.571 rad/s.\n2. The highest point on the graph gives the maximum speed: v_max = 0.6 m/s.\n3. In simple harmonic motion, the maximum acceleration is a_max = ω·v_max = 1.571 × 0.6 ≈ 0.942 m/s².\n\nThe answer is choice B (index 1), 0.942 m/s²."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xi2ZwhgYGELfokq6eEJXog","name":"submit_solution","input":{"answers":[{"item":"1","brief_reasoning":"T=4 s so ω=π/2 rad/s. v_max=0.6 m/s. a_max=ω·v_max≈0.942 m/s².","ambiguous_or_flawed":false,"choice_index":1,"final_answer":"0.942 m/s^2"}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1727,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":340,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"usage":{"input_tokens":1727,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":340,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"cost":0.0139352}
{"custom_id":"s-ap_physics_c_mechanics-f01-k1","ok":true,"model":"claude-opus-5-5","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDGus5MtiNRuhsA2Cd4P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BGmtRB7MazhzGGR6BN35L1","name":"submit_solution","input":{"answers":[{"item":"A","brief_reasoning":"Equipment: the disk on its frictionless axle, a light string wrapped around the rim, a set of known slotted masses with a hanger, a balance, and a motion detector (or a photogate on the pulley/disk, or a meterstick and stopwatch). Procedure: (1) Measure m with the balance and hang it from the string. (2) Release it from rest. (3) Record its position against time with the motion detector and take a as the slope of the velocity–time graph. If using a meterstick and stopwatch instead, time the fall through a measured height h and use a = 2h/t². (4) Change the independent variable by adding masses to the hanger, using at least 5 values of m, and repeat. To reduce uncertainty in a: do several trials for each mass and average them, or fit the slope of the v–t graph over many data points rather than using a single timing.","ambiguous_or_flawed":false,"final_answer":"Use a balance to measure m. Release m from rest and measure a with a motion detector (slope of the v–t graph), or use a = 2h/t² from a timed fall through height h. Change m by adding known masses. Reduce uncertainty by averaging several trials for each mass, or by fitting the slope of the v–t graph."},{"item":"B","brief_reasoning":"Invert the equation: 1/a = 1/g + (I/(gR²))·(1/m). This is a straight line in 1/m.","ambiguous_or_flawed":false,"final_answer":"Vertical axis: 1/a (s²/m). Horizontal axis: 1/m (kg⁻¹). Slope = I/(gR²) and intercept = 1/g."},{"item":"C","brief_reasoning":"Transformed points (1/m in kg⁻¹, 1/a in s²/m): (20, 1.626), (10, 0.862), (6.67, 0.608), (5, 0.486), (4, 0.411). Best-fit line: slope ≈ 0.076 kg·s²/m, intercept ≈ 0.105 s²/m.","ambiguous_or_flawed":false,"final_answer":"Plot 1/a (s²/m) from 0 to 1.8 against 1/m (kg⁻¹) from 0 to 22. The points lie on a straight line; the best-fit line has slope ≈ 0.076 kg·s²/m and intercept ≈ 0.10 s²/m."},{"item":"D","brief_reasoning":"Slope from points on the line: (1.626 − 0.411)/(20 − 4) ≈ 0.076 kg·s²/m. Then I = slope × g × R² = 0.076 × 9.8 × 0.01 ≈ 7.5×10⁻³ kg·m².","ambiguous_or_flawed":false,"final_answer":"I ≈ 7.5×10⁻³ kg·m²"}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":818,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1366,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":355},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"usage":{"input_tokens":818,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1366,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":355},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"cost":0.0308192}
{"custom_id":"s-ap_physics_c_mechanics-f01-k0","ok":true,"model":"claude-opus-5-5","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDGurGFygiMEB5zFBRwC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I get **I ≈ 7.6 × 10⁻³ kg·m²** for the disk. To find it, I plotted 1/a against 1/m, which gives a straight line, and used its slope. The item itself has no problems.\n\n**Part A: procedure**\n1. Equipment: the disk on its axle, light string, a set of slotted masses, a balance, and a motion detector or photogate pulley. A meterstick and stopwatch would also work.\n2. Measure each hanging mass m on the balance.\n3. Release m from rest and record its position over time.\n4. Find a, either as the slope of a velocity–time graph or from a = 2d/t² for a measured drop distance d.\n5. The independent variable is m. Change it by adding slotted masses, using five or more values from 0.05 kg to 0.25 kg.\n6. To reduce uncertainty in a, run several trials for each mass and average them. A motion sensor's velocity–time fit is also more reliable than hand timing.\n\n**Part B: axes**\nRearranging the given equation gives 1/a = 1/g + (I/(gR²))·(1/m).\n- Vertical axis: 1/a (s²/m)\n- Horizontal axis: 1/m (kg⁻¹)\n- Slope = I/(gR²), and the intercept should be close to 1/g.\n\n**Part C: plotted points**\n\n| 1/m (kg⁻¹) | 1/a (s²/m) |\n|---|---|\n| 20 | 1.645 |\n| 10 | 0.875 |\n| 6.67 | 0.616 |\n| 5 | 0.485 |\n| 4 | 0.407 |\n\nUse a horizontal scale of 0–20 kg⁻¹ and a vertical scale of 0–1.8 s²/m, then draw a best-fit straight line through the points. The line has slope ≈ 0.0774 kg·s²/m and intercept ≈ 0.097 s²/m. That intercept is close to 1/g ≈ 0.102 s²/m, which supports the model.\n\n**Part D: rotational inertia**\n- Slope = (1.645 − 0.407) / (20 − 4) ≈ 0.0774 kg·s²/m\n- I = slope × g × R² = 0.0774 × 9.8 × (0.1)² ≈ 7.6 × 10⁻³ kg·m²\n\nCheck: solving the equation directly for the m = 0.05 kg data point gives I = 0.00756 kg·m², which agrees."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018dVyMbErj3RGZdKjuhbxRv","name":"submit_solution","input":{"answers":[{"item":"A","brief_reasoning":"Measure m with a balance. Release m from rest and find a with a motion detector (slope of v-t) or from a=2d/t². Vary m with slotted masses (0.05 to 0.25 kg). Do repeated trials and average, or fit v-t, to reduce uncertainty.","final_answer":"Measure m and a for each mass, vary m with slotted masses, repeat and average trials","ambiguous_or_flawed":false},{"item":"B","brief_reasoning":"1/a = 1/g + (I/(gR²))(1/m)","final_answer":"Vertical: 1/a; horizontal: 1/m; slope = I/(gR²)","ambiguous_or_flawed":false},{"item":"C","brief_reasoning":"Points (1/m, 1/a): (20,1.645),(10,0.875),(6.67,0.616),(5,0.485),(4,0.407). The best-fit line has slope ≈0.0774 kg·s²/m and intercept ≈0.097 s²/m.","final_answer":"Linear plot of 1/a (s²/m) vs 1/m (kg⁻¹), slope ≈0.077 kg·s²/m","ambiguous_or_flawed":false},{"item":"D","brief_reasoning":"I = slope·g·R² = 0.0774×9.8×0.01","final_answer":"I ≈ 7.6×10⁻³ kg·m²","ambiguous_or_flawed":false}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":818,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1693,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":318},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"usage":{"input_tokens":818,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1693,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":318},"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"cost":0.037359199999999995}
